From: Jakub Jirutka <jakub@jirutka.cz>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:07:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip test assertions that exceed exponent range on 32-bit

The exponent of BigDecimal is a pointer-sized integer, so on 32-bit
platforms it is limited to about 2e9 decimal digits instead of 9e18.
These assertions expect results computed with the 64-bit range, but on
32-bit BigMath.exp and BigMath.erf raise FloatDomainError (Exponent
overflow) instead:

  * expm1(1e+12): exp(1e+12) has ~4e11 digits.
  * erf(10000000): not caught by the `x > 5000000000` shortcut, which
    assumes 64-bit, and then exp(1e+14) overflows.

--- a/test/bigdecimal/test_bigmath.rb
+++ b/test/bigdecimal/test_bigmath.rb
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
   PINF = BigDecimal("+Infinity")
   MINF = BigDecimal("-Infinity")
   NAN = BigDecimal("NaN")
+  # BigDecimal exponent is a pointer-sized integer, so its range is much smaller on 32-bit.
+  EXPONENT_64BIT = RbConfig::SIZEOF['void*'] >= 8
 
   def test_no_warning
     assert_separately([], "#{<<~"begin;"}\n#{<<~'end;'}")
@@ -484,7 +486,7 @@
     assert_in_exact_precision(exp(-3, 100) - 1, expm1(BigDecimal("-3"), 100), 100)
     assert_in_exact_precision(exp(BigDecimal("1.23e-10"), 120) - 1, expm1(BigDecimal("1.23e-10"), 100), 100)
     assert_in_exact_precision(exp(123, 120) - 1, expm1(BigDecimal("123"), 100), 100)
-    assert_equal(exp(BigDecimal("1e+12"), N), expm1(BigDecimal("1e+12"), N))
+    assert_equal(exp(BigDecimal("1e+12"), N), expm1(BigDecimal("1e+12"), N)) if EXPONENT_64BIT
   end
 
   def test_erf
@@ -495,7 +497,7 @@
     assert_equal(-1, BigMath.erf(MINF, N))
     assert_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(1000), 100))
     assert_equal(-1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(-1000), 100))
-    assert_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(10000000), 100))
+    assert_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(10000000), 100)) if EXPONENT_64BIT
     assert_not_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(10), 45))
     assert_not_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal(15), 100))
     assert_equal(1, BigMath.erf(BigDecimal('1e400'), 10))
